How Banks Earn From a Credit Card (Hindi narration): Mid-century Cartoon film for ExplainEveryday

Style: Mid-century Cartoon, from the Lemo-Opuscar library (https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar), drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Engine files engine/toon.js, chars.js, icons.js
are from that library's demo; engine/host.js and engine/icons2.js, film.js, kit.js, scenes_*.js, mix.py are written for this film.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by tools/fonts.sh, licence texts in fonts/)
- On screen (English): Oleo Script (Revolype), Alfa Slab One (JM Solé), Jost (indestructible type*)
- Subtitle Hindi line (Devanagari): Poppins (Indian Type Foundry); Rozha One and Kalam are loaded as fallbacks
  https://github.com/google/fonts

Voice
- Microsoft Edge neural text-to-speech, voice hi-IN-MadhurNeural (a male Hindi voice), through edge-tts (core/tts/tts_zh.py in the library). Synthetic speech.

Sound: no background music. Narration + sound effects generated by the code in this folder (stamps, pops, paper swishes, a coin ding, room tone).

Everything else (drawings, host, paper, foley) is generated by the code in this folder.
Facts on screen and in the voice-over: FACTS.md
